FILE: app/src/skip-ahead.ts
```typescript
import { updateAnimationManager } from "@babylonjs/lite";
import type { AnimationManager } from "@babylonjs/lite";

export function skipAhead(manager: AnimationManager, ms: number): void {
    updateAnimationManager(manager, ms);
}
```

I added `src/skip-ahead.ts` which delegates to `updateAnimationManager(manager, ms)` — the same entry point your game loop uses each frame, so clips, tasks, weight fades, and any enabled weighted mixers all advance together in one pass, and no manager state (including `fixedDeltaMs`) is touched, so subsequent frames are unaffected.

I'm not sure of anything; the public API surface and the doc's description of the manager lifecycle make `updateAnimationManager` the unambiguous "advance everything by one delta" call.
